// EcSurfaceOverrides.kdl
//
// Purpose:
// - Loose, user-editable routing table for EC surface-like item/static art
//   tiles that cannot be resolved automatically from `tileart.uop`,
//   `TerrainDefinition.uop`, and packed EC material provenance.
// - This file is about placed statics/items whose tileart metadata says they
//   should render like flat terrain/surface art.
// - It is not used for normal map land tiles. Use `TerrainTranscode.kdl` or
//   `EcTerrainOverrides.kdl` for map land/material behavior.
//
// Source-of-truth rule:
// - Prefer automatic routing from tileart texture refs and terrain provenance.
// - Add entries here only after manual review of unresolved, incorrectly
//   routed, or intentionally hidden surface-like static tiles.
// - This file may intentionally route EC mode back to a CC art texture when the
//   EC client has no matching material or the port is visibly incomplete.
//
// One action per CC id:
// - The parser accepts multiple action types for the same CC id, but runtime
//   priority is `cc_art`, then `ec_material`, then `ignore`.
// - Keep one active action per CC id to avoid ambiguous review state.
//
// Supported actions:
//
// 1. `cc_art` with `mode="raw-cc"`
//
//     cc_art CC_ID TARGET_CC_ID mode="raw-cc" code="reviewed_raw_cc"
//
// - Render `TARGET_CC_ID` as Classic art even while running in EC mode.
// - Use this when a tile has no acceptable EC material and the correct visual is
//   a known CC art texture.
// - `CC_ID`: source surface-like item/static id being overridden.
// - `TARGET_CC_ID`: CC art/static id to render instead.
// - `code`: optional short reason code.
//
// 2. `cc_art` with `mode="resolve-ec"`
//
//     cc_art CC_ID TARGET_CC_ID mode="resolve-ec" code="reviewed_cc_alias"
//
// - Restart EC surface resolution from `TARGET_CC_ID`.
// - Use this when the source CC id should behave like another reviewed CC tile,
//   but should still resolve to that target tile's EC material if available.
// - The resolver must reject cycles. Do not create chains such as A -> B and
//   B -> A.
//
// 3. `ec_material`
//
//     ec_material CC_ID MATERIAL_ID package="Texture.uop" code="reviewed_direct_ec_material"
//
// - Route directly to a known EC material/texture id.
// - `MATERIAL_ID`: EC material or texture id to use for this surface-like tile.
// - `package`: optional package hint. Common values:
//   - `"Texture.uop"`: normal EC WorldArt/terrain texture pool.
//   - `"LegacyTexture.uop"`: EC legacy tileart texture pool.
//   - `"TerrainTexture.uop"`: support texture pool. Do not use as visible
//     albedo unless manual review proves that specific texture is visible art.
// - `code`: optional short reason code.
//
// 4. `ignore`
//
//     ignore CC_ID code="not_ported_to_ec"
//
// - Treat the tile as transparent/no-render.
// - Use this for reviewed not-ported, intentionally hidden, or placeholder
//   cases. Do not use it to mask parser bugs.
//
// Supported `mode` keywords:
// - `"raw-cc"`: render the target as CC art.
// - `"resolve-ec"`: use the target id as an alias and run EC resolution.
// - Any other string parses as unknown and should be treated as invalid by
//   audit/runtime policy.
//
// Reason code guidance:
// - Keep `code` values short and enumerable. Audits emit this as `reason_code`.
// - Suggested initial codes:
//   - `unmatched_ec_port`
//   - `reviewed_cc_alias`
//   - `reviewed_raw_cc`
//   - `reviewed_direct_ec_material`
//   - `intentionally_hidden`
//   - `not_ported_to_ec`
//   - `manual_visual_match`
//   - `source_material_missing`
//
// Relationship to other KDL files:
// - `TerrainTranscode.kdl` maps CC land ids to EC terrain/runtime slots.
// - `EcTerrainOverrides.kdl` modifies/integrates EC terrain material behavior.
// - `EcSurfaceOverrides.kdl` handles item/static surface-like art routing.
//
// Unmatched candidates from the 2026-05-19 FP audit. Uncomment and choose an
// action only after manual visual review.
//
// ignore 39698 code="unmatched_ec_port"
//
// ignore 39699 code="unmatched_ec_port"
//
// ignore 39700 code="unmatched_ec_port"
//
// ignore 39805 code="unmatched_ec_port"
